        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A person who belongs to the sex that normally produces sperm. The term is used to indicate biological sex distinctions, cultural gender role distinctions, or both. (NCI)
 A person who belongs to the sex that normally produces sperm. The term is used to indicate biological sex distinctions, cultural gender role distinctions, or both. (NCI) (NCI)
 Male
 (HL7V3.0)
 Used for all-male populations when sex is pertinent to the focus of the study. For comparison of sexes use HUMAN SEX DIFFERENCES. (PSY)
 Use in conjunction with a disease, disorder, dysfunction, body system, or function which is gender specific. (CSP)
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0086582</skos:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C0086582</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Organism Attribute</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


