    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/BSO_AD#00142">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/BSO_AD#00139"/>
        <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Poverty</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A situation in which the level of living of an individual, family, or group is below the standard of the community. It is often related to a specific income level. (MSH)
 A subjective and comparative term describing a lack of sufficient wealth (usually understood as capital, money, material goods, or resources especially natural resources) to live what is understood in a society as a &quot;normal&quot; life: for instance, to be capable of raising a healthy family, and especially educating children and participating in society. A person living in this condition of poverty is said to be poor. The meaning of &quot;sufficient&quot; varies widely across the different political and economic areas of the world. (NCI)
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0032854</skos:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C0032854</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Group Attribute</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


