        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Coverage by contract whereby one part indemnifies or guarantees another against loss by a specified contingency. (MSH)
 A mechanism for guarding against financial aspects of risk by making payments in the form of premiums to an insurance company, which pays an agreed-upon sum to the insured in the event of loss. (NCI)
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0021672</skos:definition>
