        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Educational attainment or level of education of an individual. (MSH)
 Highest level of education that a person has attained. (NCI)
 Highest education attained. (NCI)
 An indication of the years of schooling completed in graded public, private, or parochial schools, and in colleges, universities, or professional schools. (NCI)
 Completion of a course of study or reaching a specific educational level. (PSY)
 The magnitude or quantity of training considered in relation to an arbitrary reference value. (CSP)
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0013658</skos:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C0013658</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Finding</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


