        <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Neighborhood_Concentrated_Disadvantage</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Neighborhood Disadvantage</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Neighborhood disadvantage refers to the lack of economic and social resources in a neighborhood and has been shown to exert a detrimental effect on health outcomes over and above individual level characteristics. (MSH)
 The recognition that low neighborhood socioeconomic conditions have an impact on the services and opportunities available to its residents and have a wide and long-lasting effect on their economic, social and educational development. U.S. Census data can be used to determine the concentration of poverty at the neighborhood level. (NCI)
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C2985113</skos:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C2985113</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Idea or Concept</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


